# Never Rewrite Active League History

Active leagues are in progress at all times. League matchups, standings, playoff seeds,
and brackets are NOT persisted — they are recomputed on the fly from deterministic
algorithms (see `lib/leagueMatchups.ts`) plus stored weekly scores. This means any change
to those algorithms retroactively rewrites past matchups, W-L records, seeds, and playoff
brackets for every existing league.

## Rules

- When refactoring or generalizing schedule/seeding/playoff logic, the new code MUST
  produce byte-for-byte identical output to the old code for all league shapes that
  already exist in production (e.g. 8-team H2H). Verify by diffing new output against
  a copy of the legacy algorithm across all rounds before shipping (see the incident:
  the round-robin rotation and seed tiebreaker were changed during the 4–8 team
  generalization, which reshuffled a live league's records and semifinal matchups).
- Deterministic details that silently define league history and must never change for
  existing leagues: sort order of member IDs (lexicographic), rotation direction/method
  of the round-robin, seed tiebreakers (wins, losses, ties, total points, then
  lexicographic user ID), and playoff pairing order (1v8, 4v5, 2v7, 3v6).
- New behavior is fine for NEW league shapes or NEW seasons, but must be gated so
  existing leagues keep their original computation (e.g. by season slug, league size,
  or a stored config flag) unless the user explicitly asks to change live leagues.
- If a change unavoidably affects active leagues, call it out explicitly to the user
  before shipping and get confirmation.
